output([{"序号": "1","姓名": "张伟楠","单位": "上海交通大学","日期，时间，地点": "2022.10.17\\n16:00-17:30\\nLecture Theatre 2\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "从特征交互到样本交互：表格数据深度学习的新趋势","讲座或活动内容": "为助力澳门创新科技发展，加强大数据及医学人工智能在澳门的发展及推广，澳门理工大学应用科学学院举办了跨领域的大数据及医学人工智能主题讲座，由上海交通大学副教授张伟楠主讲“从特征交互到样本交互：表格数据深度学习的新趋势”。讲座中，张伟楠表示大数据和深度学习技术为人们的日常生活赋能，数据科学面临着新的挑战，传统的深度学习模型难以有效地从非感知数据中挖掘高阶交互模式，针对此难点，他介绍了相应的创新性的解决方法，并简要回顾迄今为止在表格数据上的深度学习模型的发展，重点是探索每个样本的特征交互模式，并提供推荐系统的运行案例。最后总结一种新的深度学习范式并讨论其未来的发展和应用。","个人简介": "张伟楠现为上海交通大学副教授。他的研究兴趣包括强化学习、深度学习和数据科学，以及推荐系统、搜索引擎、文本挖掘和生成、游戏人工智能等的各种现实应用。他在国际会议和期刊上发表了100多篇研究论文。他的研究获得了SIGD最佳论文荣誉奖之2017年DLP最佳论文奖嗣2019年KDD研讨会和2020年CoRL最佳系统论文奖。"},{"序号": "2","姓名": "沈定刚","单位": "上海理工大学医学院，中国上海联合成像智能有限公司","日期，时间，地点": "2023.3.31\\n11:00-12:00\\nLecture Theatre 3\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "快速开发和部署用于实际医疗应用的 AI 技术","讲座或活动内容": "在本次讲座中，沈教授介绍了全栈、全谱人工智能（AI，或深度学习）技术，用于使用多模态数据，从数据采集到疾病检测、随访、诊断、治疗和结果预测（或评估），用于整个临床工作流程。展示扫描仪和临床管线中创新技术开发和实施的细节（即用于快速 MR、低剂量 CT/PET 采集和临床诊断/治疗），并与其他最先进的技术进行比较。","个人简介": "沈定刚是上海科技大学生物医学工程学院教授、创始院长，上海联影智能（UII）联席首席执行官。他是IEEE、美国医学与生物工程学会（AIMBE）、国际模式识别协会（IAPR）和医学图像计算和计算机辅助干预（MICCAI）学会的会员。他是美国北卡罗来纳州教堂山市北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校 （UNC-CH） 的 Jeffrey Houpt 杰出研究员和全职教授（终身教授），负责指导图像分析和信息学中心、图像显示、增强和分析 （IDEA） 实验室和医学图像分析核心。他还曾是宾夕法尼亚大学（宾夕法尼亚大学）的终身助理教授，以及约翰霍普金斯大学的讲师。他的研究兴趣包括医学图像分析、机器学习、深度学习和计算机视觉。他在国际期刊和会议论文集上发表了 1500 多篇同行评审论文，H指数 128 次，引用次数超过 70K。他担任《放射学前沿》（Frontiers in Radiology）的主编，以及八种国际期刊的副主编（或编委会成员）。此外，他还曾在 2012-2015 年担任医学图像计算和计算机辅助干预 （MICCAI） 协会的董事会成员，并担任 MICCAI 2019 的主席。"},{"序号": "3","姓名": "袁峰","单位": "广州软件应用技术研究院","日期，时间，地点": "2023.9.27\\n15:00-16:00\\nTheatre 2\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "关于科研成果产业化工作与实践的思考","讲座或活动内容": "本次讲座介绍团队了的工作成果，探讨如何将科研与产业化有效融合，解决脱节问题，跨越技术创新的“死亡之谷”。袁教授结合实际工作，分享经验、教训和思考。","个人简介": "袁峰博士，现任广州软件应用执行副总裁丁技术研究所，中国科学院软件研究所软件开发研究部副主任。兼任工信部智慧城市产业联盟专家、住房城乡建设部智慧城市专家、中国软件过程改进协会副秘书长、中国通信行业协会物联网专家委员会委员、广东省重大行政决策咨询论证专家、广东省数据专家、专家委员会委员，广东省、广州市科技专家库专家、华南理工大学EMBA导师等，主持完成智慧城市多条产业线技术攻关。先后荣获巴塞罗那智慧城市国际博览会创新总决赛奖、中国物联网关键技术创新奖、广东省科技进步三等奖、广州市科技进步三等奖，荣获广州市高层次人才、广州市最美科技作品获得者和第十届“金手指奖”中国照明行业领袖奖等称号。"},{"序号": "4","姓名": "倪东","单位": "深圳大学医学部生物医学工程学院","日期，时间，地点": "2024.2.20","题目或主题": "澳门参与胎儿超声波智能化科研","讲座或活动内容": "澳门理工大学、镜湖医院、南光医疗管理顾问有限公司（南光医疗）、深圳度影医疗科技有限公司及深圳大学，在澳门理工大学举办“胎儿超声智能质量控制标准、关键技术及示范应用研究”科研项目启动式。活动上，项目澳门区负责人、理工大学应用科学学院副教授檀韬，深圳大学生物医学工程学院教授倪东，镜湖医院影像科副主任李峻，深圳度影医疗科技有限公司经理胡歆迪，南光医疗副总经理蔡惠仪等，从不同角度发表演讲课题。据悉，研究团队目标藉这次项目，构建产前超声质量控制标准研究和多中心数据集、产前超声智能质控与培训关键技术研究，以及智能质控和培训系统的开发、部署、优化与示范应用，以推动产前超声质量控制的标准化、智能化水平。项目预计为期两年，通过当地临床实验和认证，在项目结题后两年至四年内投入市场使用，目标覆盖中国内地、澳门、香港的妇产科室。临床医生将利用研发的系统，在孕检者检测过程中实现包含切面识别、结构检测、产前报告全方位产前超声智能分析。从根本上解决“产前超声检查同质化水平低”、“人工超声质控无法实时评价”、“基层医院难以大面积推广高水平诊断技术”、“三甲等高水平医院看病难”等临床和社会难题。","个人简介": "倪東，博士，教授，深圳大学医学部生物医学工程学院副院长，人工智能医疗影像国际顶级会议MICCAI理事会成员，国家重点研发计划首席科学家，广东省超声医学工程学会副会长，中国生物医学工程学会人工智能专委会青委会副主任委员，中国医学装备协会超声技术分会大数据与人工智能专委会副主任委员，广东省医疗行业协会超声医学创新与发展管理分会副主任委员，深圳大学优秀学者。分别于2000年和2003年获东南大学生物医学工程学士与硕士学位，2009年获香港中文大学博士学位。2003至2006年在深圳迈瑞公司超声研发部工作，2009年至2010年在美国北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校从事博士后研究，自2010年4月开始在深圳大学工作。获评深圳海外高层次人才孔雀计划B类人才（2018）、C类人才（2015）。获得深圳市科学技术进步奖一等奖（2019），吴文俊人工智能科学技术奖三等奖（2018）。"},{"序号": "5","姓名": "王珊珊","单位": "中国科学院深圳先进技术研究院","日期，时间，地点": "2024.2.29\\n16:00-18:00\\nTheatre 3\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "用于医学成像的 AI 基础模型","讲座或活动内容": "广义医学人工智能（AI）的基础模型最近引起了极大的关注，并在改变医疗保健方面具有巨大的潜力。与当前的医学人工智能模型不同，基础模型有望解决各种各样的具有挑战性的任务，同时几乎不需要甚至不需要特定任务的标签。医学成像是一个仍然存在大量技术和临床挑战的研究领域。人工智能，特别是深度学习（DL），在解决这些挑战方面表现出了很高的潜力。然而，当前的DL方法仍然是针对特定任务的，并且缺乏泛化能力。本次演讲探讨医学成像的基础模型。一个主要目的是探索医学成像中基础概念和临床相关挑战之间的联系。主题涵盖了快速MR成像和图像后处理，如图像分割和分类。演讲最后讨论与医学成像特别相关的基础模型中的悬而未决的问题，以及这一新兴领域的潜在挑战和机遇。","个人简介": "王珊珊博士是中国科学院Paul C Lauterbur研究中心的教授，她致力于开发新的自适应学习方法和应用程序，用于快速医学成像和智能医学分析。凭借生物医学工程（BME）和计算机科学（CS）的双博士学位，她率先将核心CS方法与成像科学相结合。她的创新方法为医学成像领域做出了几项重要贡献。王博士曾任Gordon全体讲师、NIBIB New Horizons全体讲师、IEEE高级会员、OCSMRM BoT/Life会员、《医学磁共振》副主编、《IEEE医学成像、模式识别与生物医学信号处理与控制汇刊》副主编等职。她还被美国斯坦福大学选为2022-2024年世界前2%科学家。"},{"序号": "6","姓名": "王鑫","单位": "Netherlands Cancer Institute (NKI), Amsterdam, The Netherlands","日期，时间，地点": "2024.4.12\\n14:30-15:30\\nA202\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "An Explainable Longitudinal Multi-modal Fusion Model for Predicting Neoadjuvant\\nTherapy Response in Breast Cancer Treatment","讲座或活动内容": "In this study, Gao et al. aimed to develop and validate an AI multi-modal model, named\\nMulti-modal Response Prediction (MRP), to predict pathological complete response (pCR)\\nusing longitudinal information of patient records across the neoadjuvant therapy (NAT)\\ncare scenarios, including Pre-NAT(Staging), Mid-NAT, and Post-NAT(Pre-surgical). The\\nsystem's clinical impact analysis revealed that MRP has the potential to optimize\\npersonalized treatment decisions, considering both clinician and patient preferences.\\nThe system's clinical impact analysis revealed that MRP has the potential to optimize\\npersonalized treatment decisions, taking into account both clinician and patient\\npreferences.","个人简介": null},{"序号": "7","姓名": "高原","单位": "Netherlands Cancer Institute (NKI), Amsterdam, The Netherlands","日期，时间，地点": "2024.4.12\\n15:30-16:30\\nA202\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "MTP-BCR: Predicting Long Term Breast Cancer Risk Using Longitudinal Mammographic\\nScreening History","讲座或活动内容": "In this study, Wang et al. presented the multi-time-points breast cancer risk (MTP-BCR)\\nmodel, a novel temporospatial DL risk model that integrates traditional BC risk\\nfactors and longitudinal mammography data to identify subtle changes in breast tissue\\nindicative of future malignancy. This model demonstrates a significant improvement in\\nup to 10-year risk prediction with an AUC of 0.80 and outperforms the traditional and\\nDL risk methods in both screening and recurrence cohorts. Moreover, MTP-BCR provides\\nunilateral breast-level predictions with AUCs up to 0.81 and 0.77 for 5-year and 10-\\nyear risk assessments, respectively. Further validation in the public CSAW-CC dataset\\ndemonstrates the consistent advantage of our method compared to the single-time pointbased\\nmodel.","个人简介": null},{"序号": "8","姓名": "李硕","单位": null,"日期，时间，地点": "2024.7.11\\n16:00-18:00\\nLecture Theatre 1\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "Ai to eliminate chemical contrast agent in imaging","讲座或活动内容": "Chemical contrast agent-enhanced imaging plays a critical role in clinical diagnostic imaging. Recently there has been an increasing concern regarding the chemical contrast agent used in the clinic. In this talk, Dr. Li will share his ground-breaking AI contrast-enhanced imaging, which develops state-of-the-art machine-learning techniques to eliminate the need for chemical contrast agents.","个人简介": "Global leader in AI clinical imaging research.MICCAI board member and MICCAI 2022 conference chair.Over 200 publications and editor of six Springer books."},{"序号": "9","姓名": "张俭嘉","单位": "Associate Professor at the School of Biomedical Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University.\\n","日期，时间，地点": "2024.10.21\\n16:00-18:00\\nLecture Theatre 2\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": "Dynamic Construction and Analysis of Brain \\nFunctional Networks Based on Deep Learning","讲座或活动内容": "Patients with brain diseases like Alzheimer's (AD) are numerous and currently incurable. Early\\nintervention is the most effective treatment, but precise early diagnostic techniques for AD are\\nlacking. Constructing and analyzing brain functional networks (FBN) using resting-state fMRI (rs_x0002_fMRI) is a key tool for early AD diagnosis. However, current FBN methods lack flexibility, resolution,\\nand fail to fully utilize rs-fMRI’s temporal information, limiting diagnostic accuracy. This report\\nexplores dynamic, multi-level FBN construction using advanced deep learning frameworks to\\nenhance spatiotemporal resolution, improving early AD diagnosis and advancing its clinical\\napplication.","个人简介": "Dr.Zhang is an Associate Professor at Sun Yat-sen University’s School of Biomedical Engineering. His\\nresearch focuses on computer vision and functional brain networks, with over 40 papers published\\nin top journals and conferences like IEEE TPAMI, IEEE TMI, and CVPR. He has led several projects\\nfunded by the National Natural Science Foundation of China and local foundations.\\nPreviously, Zhang was a postdoctoral researcher at CSIRO and a lecturer at the University of\\nTechnology Sydney, where he led data science projects. He was part of the team that won the 2018\\nAustralian \"Eureka\" Prize for Data Science and the Australian Water Association’s Research\\nInnovation Award."},{"序号": "10","姓名": "梁兴龙","单位": "Ph.D. student at the Ritse Mann's Breast lmaging Group (BlG) in RadbouduMC and Regina Beets-Tan's group in theRadiology Department of the Netherlands Cancer Institute","日期，时间，地点": "2024.3.10\\n11:30-12:30\\nA202\\nCHI UN Building","题目或主题": "FDG PET-CT Guided Explainable Multi-OmicsDeep Learning Model for Long-term BreastCancer Prognosis","讲座或活动内容": "FDG PET-CTis widely used in breast cancermanagement, providing both anatomical and metabolic insightsHowever, traditional prognostic assessments based on predefined imaging parameters (e.g., SUVmax, MTV,TLG) may fail to capture the full complexity of PET-CT data. To enhance long-term prognosis, we propose aintegrates FDG PET-CTdeep-learning-based Multi-Omics PrognosticStratification(MOPs)modelthatclinical data, and medical reports to predict overall survival (OS) and disease-free survival (DfS) in non.metastatic breast cancer patients. Using a Transformer-based cross-modal attention mechanism, the modeperforms multi-omics fusion and incorporates explainable Al technigues, including causal analysisvisualization, and semantic explanations. Experimental results demonstrate that MOPs outperforms singleomics models in survival prediction, effectively stratifies patients into high- and low-risk groups, andprovides more comprehensive prognostic insights beyond TNM staging and molecular subtyping. Byenhancing model interpretability, MOPS improves clinical transparency, supporting oncologists inoptimizing treatment strategies and improving patient outcomes.","个人简介": "Dr. Liang obtained his master's degree from Harbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen) in 2021. in 2023, hejoined Ritse Mann's Breast lmaging Group (BlG) in RadboudUMC and Regina Beets-Tan's group in theRadiology Department of the Netherlands Cancer Institute as a PhD student, His research interests includedeep learning in breast imaging and multimodal deep learning models based on PET/CT etc."},{"序号": "11","姓名": "Dr. Ritse Mann","单位": "Principal Investigator Radboud University Medical Center\\nChair of breast imaging the Netherlands Cancer Institute\\nChairperson of the scientific committee of the European Society of Breast lmaging\\nPresident of the Dutch Breast lmaging Academy","日期，时间，地点": "2024.4.22\\n15:30 – 17:30\\nA311, 3F\\nCHI UN Building","题目或主题": "Academic Writing Guide: Writing Papers for Prestigious International Journals","讲座或活动内容": "In the era of rapid technological advancement, artificial intelligence has significantly transformed the landscape of breast imaging research, making diagnostic tools more precise and efficient.\\nHowever, translating innovative AI methods into impactful academic publications requires a strategic approach. I will briefly introduce how to select the appropriate journal, how to structure the manuscript to meet journal requirements, and how to craft a compelling narrative that highlights the scientific and clinical relevance of the research. Additionally, the importance of the peer-review process, how to effectively respond to reviewers' comments, and maintaining transparency and reproducibility in research will be emphasized. By following these strategies,\\nresearchers can enhance the impact of their work, increase the chances of successful publication, and make meaningful contributions to the field of breast imaging and AI integration.","个人简介": "Dr. Ritse Mann is a dedicated breast and interventional radiologist at Radboudumc. He is an expert in breast imaging, with a particular focus on breast MRI, and is the scientific leader of the clinical breast research group that focuses on the clinical validation of novel strategies for breast cancer detection and treatment. Ritse Mann is the Principal Investigator at Radboud University Medical\\nCenter, Chair of Breast Imaging at the Netherlands Cancer Institute, Chairperson of the Scientific\\nCommittee of the European Society of Breast Imaging, and President of the Dutch Breast Imaging\\nAcademy. He is an international authority in breast imaging, interventional radiology, and AI diagnostics. He serves as Associate Editor for Radiology and Editorial Board Member for European\\nRadiology, H-index: 62, with over 15,900 citations."},{"序号": "12","姓名": "Prof. Huazhu Fu","单位": "Principal Scientist at the Institute of High Performance Computing (IHPC), Agency for Science, Technology and Research (A*STAR), Singapore. Associate Editor for top journals (including IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI), among others). Expert in AI for Medical Image Analysis and Healthcare.","日期，时间，地点": "2025.7.29\\n20:00-21:00\\nTencent Meeting：263-388-447","题目或主题": "Torwards Clinician-Friendly AI for Better Clinical Uses","讲座或活动内容": "Dr. Huazhu Fu is a Principal Scientist at A*STAR’s Institute of High Performance Computing (IHPC) in \\nSingapore, specializing in Medical Image Analysis, AI for Healthcare, and Trustworthy AI. He has \\npublished over 200 papers in leading journals and conferences, such as *Nature Machine \\nIntelligence*, *Nature Communications*, *IEEE TPAMI*, and *IEEE TMI*, with more than 25,000 \\ncitations on Google Scholar. His work has earned him multiple awards, including Best Paper at ICME \\n2021, MICCAI-OMIA 2022, and MICCAI-DeCAF 2023. He also serves as an Associate Editor for \\nseveral journals, including *IEEE TMI*, *IEEE TNNLS*, *Pattern Recognition*, *IEEE TAI*, and *IEEE \\nJBHI*. More information can be found at [https://hzfu.github.io]","个人简介": "Dr. Huazhu Fu is a Principal Scientist at A*STAR’s Institute of High Performance Computing (IHPC) in \\nSingapore, specializing in Medical Image Analysis, AI for Healthcare, and Trustworthy AI. He has \\npublished over 200 papers in leading journals and conferences, such as *Nature Machine \\nIntelligence*, *Nature Communications*, *IEEE TPAMI*, and *IEEE TMI*, with more than 25,000 \\ncitations on Google Scholar. His work has earned him multiple awards, including Best Paper at ICME \\n2021, MICCAI-OMIA 2022, and MICCAI-DeCAF 2023. He also serves as an Associate Editor for \\nseveral journals, including *IEEE TMI*, *IEEE TNNLS*, *Pattern Recognition*, *IEEE TAI*, and *IEEE \\nJBHI*. More information can be found at [https://hzfu.github.io]"},{"序号": "13","姓名": " Prof. Boxin Shi","单位": "Associate Professor and Reasearch Professor at Peking University","日期，时间，地点": "2025.7.28\\n10:30-11:30\\nLecture Theatre 3\\nWuiChi Building","题目或主题": " Controllable Visual Content Repainting","讲座或活动内容": "Controllable visual content repainting aims to deeply understand user instructions across different modal representations, thereby creating images or videos that meet specific needs and creative expressions. This talk will introduce two advancements in controllable visual repainting. To control physical attribute in image generation, we propose Phys-EdiT, which enables joint control of material properties, lighting conditions, and semantic elements of instances in images, supporting pixel-level continuous attribute adjustments. To control temporal editing in video generation, we introduce VIRES, which achieves cross-frame motion consistency and pixel-level sketch alignment in tasks such as video instance repainting, replacement, generation, and removal through temporal attention reorganization and sketch semantic injection mechanisms. These works enhance the ability of existing diffusion models to precisely control specific attributes, offering new perspectives for building highly controllable visual content generation models.","个人简介": "Boxin Shi is currently a Boya Young Fellow Associate Professor (with tenure) and Research Professor at Peking University, where he leads the Camera Intelligence Lab. He received the PhD degree from the University of Tokyo in 2013. From 2013 to 2017, he did research at MIT Media Lab, Singapore University of Technology and Design, Nanyang Technological University, and National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology. His research interests are computational photography and computer vision. He has published more than 200 papers, including 30 papers in TPAMI and 100+ papers in CVPR/ICCV/ECCV. His papers were awarded as Best Paper, Runners-Up at CVPR 2024/ICCP 2015, and selected as candidate for Best Paper at ICCV 2015. He received the Okawa Foundation Research Grant in 2021. He has served as an associate editor of TAPMI/IJCV and an area chair of CVPR/ICCV/ECCV. He is a Distinguished Lecturer of APSIPA, a Distinguished Member of CCF, and a Senior Member of the IEEE/CSIG, and. Please access his lab website for more information: http ://camera.pku.edu.cn"}])